 {:entry/name        "Dark Elves"
  :entry/type        :entry.type/race
  :entry/description "In the language of _Aman_ all _Elves_ that did not cross the _Great Sea_ were Dark Elves, and the term is sometimes used thus; when _Caranthir_ called _Thingol_ a _Dark Elf_ it was intended opprobriously, and was especially so, since _Thingol_ had been to _Aman_ and was not accounted among them. But in the period of the Exile of the _Noldor_ it was often used of the _Elves_ of _Middle-earth_ other than the _Noldor_ and the _Sindar_, and is then virtually equivalent to _Avari_. Different again is the title _Dark Elf_ of the _Sindarin_ Elf _Eöl_; but in one passage _Turgon_ no doubt meant that _Eöl_ was a _Dark Elf_ in the first sense."
  :entry/page        [42 46 81 94 98 102 114 124 126 128 132 192]
  :entry/appears-in  [[:chapter/name "Of the Coming of the Elves and the Captivity of Melkor"]
                      [:chapter/name "Of Thingol and Melian"]
